well it's been one year since Nevada  state trooper Micah May was killed in  the line of duty the 46 year old was hit  by an impaired driver during a chase on  the I-15 well now law enforcement  agencies across the state are coming  together to remember him and keep  everyone safe on the road Sasha Loftus  filed this report earlier tonight  he was definitely my rock one year after  Nevada Highway Patrol Trooper Micah May  lost his life his wife Joanna shares  what she loved most about him he was  very funny very witty and extremely  smart Trooper May died in the line of  duty on July 29 2021 when an impaired  driver hit him during a chase on the  I-15  officer on Friday family friends and law  enforcement gathered to honor him and  mark the start of an annual Statewide  initiative his life was taken from us  from an impaired driver and so it's just  that much more special to us that we go  out there and we save lives Nevada State  Police Trooper Ashley Wellman says the  goal of the may you choose not to drive  impaired campaign is to get drivers who  are under the influence off the road and  keep others safe today is truly  Bittersweet but the beauty in the  tragedy is that we've all come together  all while remembering the man Micah May  was behind the batch he was an amazing  husband and father and supporting those  he cared for most every single day I  I'm so grateful that Nevada Highway  Patrol actually stuck to their guns and  is there to help us when we need them  Sasha Loftus live local now
 

